      "head_repo": "Lumnus/B70-LLM-Controller",
      "url": "https://github.com/wu1ff/B70-LLM-Controller/pull/4",
      "commit_message": "Flash-Next Base: 1024-token prefill chunk, 16 slots, power-of-two captures\n\nBase mode now launches with --max-num-batched-tokens 1024, --max-num-seqs 16\nand cudagraph capture sizes [1,2,4,8,16,256,512,1024]. The three flags move\nfrom the shared runtime layer to the mode layer so MTP3 keeps exactly the\nqualified 256 / 4 / [1,2,4,8,256]; the rendered MTP3 commands carry the same\nflags and values as before (argument order only). Utilisation unchanged.\n\nMeasured on 4x Arc Pro B70 with this checkpoint: prefill 2,674 -> 4,711\ntok/s at 18.7K and 1,686 -> 3,711 tok/s at 98K, decode and MMLU/TruthfulQA\nunchanged; chat-mix aggregate 181/289/364/425 tok/s at 4/8/12/16\nconcurrent. README documents the measurements and why capture sizes must\nstay powers of two.\n\nPack version and the catalog entry are left unchanged for the maintainer's\nrelease step.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"
    },
    "5": {
      "head_commit": "3e7f3cec3c5c2a4cf6f0929f5620293631b93471",
      "single_commit": true,
      "base_commit": "e068298e1270086d04b324b2b66ddbd5f6b3efd4",
      "state": "open",
      "merged": false,
      "author": "KaloyanNaumov",
      "head_repo": "Lumnus/B70-LLM-Controller",
      "url": "https://github.com/wu1ff/B70-LLM-Controller/pull/5",
      "commit_message": "Flash-Next patches 008-012 (proposed): INT8 PLE table, optionally from NVMe\n\nFive opt-in vLLM patches on top of the 1.0.2 tree, all off by default:\n008 fills the pinned PLE slabs straight from the memory-mapped table\n(boot host-RAM peak ~191 -> ~158 GiB on 4 ranks); 009 FP8 table loader\n(carried as a dependency of 010, not a recommended mode); 010 INT8 table\nwith one fp32 scale per row (48.9 GiB pinned instead of 95.4 GiB BF16) and\nits build recipe; 011/012 serve that INT8 table from NVMe through a small\npinned row cache, with a native reader.\n\nEach directory follows the pack's patch format (plain unified diff, README\nwith the nine fields); SHA256SUMS and the patch index are updated. Applying\n008-012 to the 1.0.2 tree gives files byte-identical to the series we\nserve. Pack version, catalog entry and the runtime image are left to the\nmaintainer's release step.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"
    },
    "6": {
      "head_commit": "f5db99eeb3526038356caaf6746445d1e4a60c88",
      "single_commit": true,
      "base_commit": "e068298e1270086d04b324b2b66ddbd5f6b3efd4",
      "state": "open",
      "merged": false,
      "author": "KaloyanNaumov",
      "head_repo": "Lumnus/B70-LLM-Controller",
      "url": "https://github.com/wu1ff/B70-LLM-Controller/pull/6",
      "commit_message": "Flash-Next patches 020-022 (proposed): chat API helpers, all opt-in\n\n020 B70_THINKING_BUDGET caps reasoning tokens by the effort the client asked\nfor (a request's own thinking_token_budget wins) and B70_DEFAULT_PRESENCE_PENALTY\nsets a server default; 021 B70_DEFAULT_REPETITION_DETECTION sets a server\ndefault for vLLM's repetition stop; 022 B70_REASONING_EFFORT_ALIAS maps an\nOpenRouter-style reasoning.effort onto reasoning_effort. Only the chat\nrequest protocol is touched; the one ungated change is that\nreasoning_effort also accepts \"ultra\".\n\nPlain unified diffs in the pack's patch format; SHA256SUMS and the patch\nindex updated. Independent of the other proposed patches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"
    },
    "7": {
      "head_commit": "c08f93c376a91353f69761c0ccc9b4dbebed1bd6",
      "single_commit": true,
      "base_commit": "e068298e1270086d04b324b2b66ddbd5f6b3efd4",
      "state": "open",
      "merged": false,
      "author": "KaloyanNaumov",
      "head_repo": "Lumnus/B70-LLM-Controller",
      "url": "https://github.com/wu1ff/B70-LLM-Controller/pull/7",
      "commit_message": "Flash-Next patch 023 (proposed): skip indexer tensors on dense-QSA configs\n\nDense-QSA configs build no indexer module, but some checkpoints still ship\nself_attn.indexer.* tensors inside mixed shards (e.g. the calibrated AWQ\nexport wtdcode/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-AWQ-W4A16 at 0939125), and the loader\nfails with \"There is no module or parameter named ...\". Skip them the same\nway the PLE hashstats_/token_lookup columns are skipped. Inert on the\npinned devan-carlin revision.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"
    },
    "8": {
      "head_commit": "560c766af3d5ecc03fe369a2ef9a444cea76b359",
      "single_commit": true,
      "base_commit": "e068298e1270086d04b324b2b66ddbd5f6b3efd4",
      "state": "open",
      "merged": false,
      "author": "KaloyanNaumov",
      "head_repo": "Lumnus/B70-LLM-Controller",
      "url": "https://github.com/wu1ff/B70-LLM-Controller/pull/8",
      "commit_message": "Flash-Next patches 013-019 (proposed): hybrid KV-offload miss fix, chunked pinned pool\n\nWith the CPU KV offload tier, a hybrid (full attention + GDN) model keeps one\nGDN state per request at round_down(L-1, block). A revisit whose suffix\nchanges before that boundary returns 0 hit tokens for the whole request,\nand because the offload lookup never sets a shared-prefix junction the\nrecompute stores its state inside the changed suffix again: the prefix\nmisses on every revisit. 014 (B70_OFFLOAD_JUNCTION=1) heals it after one\nmiss, 015 (B70_OFFLOAD_GDN_BACKSTEP=N) prevents the first miss; 013 adds\nopt-in tracing; 016-018 carry the guard for vllm#56795 and a gated backport\nof vllm#51787 (both off in what we serve). 019 stores the pinned CPU pool as\nrow-aligned chunks when one allocation is refused (>= ~31 GiB per rank on a\nB70), instead of failing at boot.\n\nPlain unified diffs in the pack's patch format with READMEs, CPU tests\nincluded as separate (not applied) patches; SHA256SUMS and the patch index\nupdated. Independent of 008-012. Applying all proposed patches to the 1.0.2\ntree gives files byte-identical to the series we serve.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"
    }
  },
